<title>BELGIUM: Top 15 Belgian companies in planned FT index.</title>
<headline>Top 15 Belgian companies in planned FT index.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brussels top 15 companies in terms of market capitalisation will be included in the new pan-European Eurotop 300 index due to be launched in July by the Financial Times and Amsterdam Exchanges, the Dutch bourse group said on Friday.</p>
<p>As at March 31, 1997, the Belgian members of the Eurotop 300 were (in order given):</p>
<p>Banque Bruxelles Lambert, Fortis AG, Generale Bank, Societe Generale de Belgique, Groupe Bruxelles Lambert, Kredietbank, Royale Belge, Solvay, UCB, Electrafina, PetroFina, Delhaize, Electrabel, Powerfin and Tractebel.</p>
<p>The composition by the launch date may have changed, given plans by Powerfin and Tractebel to merge.</p>
<p>The Financial Times said existing indices, such as the FT S&amp;P European and Morgan Stanley Capital International (MSCI), were not useful for derivatives.</p>
<p>The Amsterdam Exchanges plans to launch a series of options based on the new index.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
